WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.826
"Dad," Ricky said one day.

2
00:00:07.826 --> 00:00:14.860
"When I grow up, I want to be an Arctic explorer."

3
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.816
"Really?" said Dad. "Why?"

4
00:00:18.816 --> 00:00:23.019
"The Arctic is so cool!" said Ricky.

5
00:00:23.019 --> 00:00:26.253
"We learned about it in class.

6
00:00:26.253 --> 00:00:32.070
I want to see polar bears and Arctic foxes."

7
00:00:32.071 --> 00:00:34.955
"That's great," said Dad.

8
00:00:34.955 --> 00:00:37.913
"But can you live there?"

9
00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:40.920
Ricky thought about it for a while.

10
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.907
"Is living in the Arctic very hard?" he asked.

11
00:00:45.907 --> 00:00:48.011
"Yes," said Dad.

12
00:00:48.011 --> 00:00:52.056
"Did you know it's always light during summer?"

13
00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:54.327
"No," said Ricky.

14
00:00:54.327 --> 00:00:57.332
"But that would be awesome!"

15
00:00:57.332 --> 00:01:01.643
"And it's always dark during winter," said Dad.

16
00:01:01.643 --> 00:01:04.299
"Oh," said Ricky.

17
00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:07.007
"That's not so awesome."

18
00:01:07.007 --> 00:01:11.283
"It gets very cold in the Arctic," Dad continued.

19
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:15.152
"Hot water can turn to ice right away!"

20
00:01:15.152 --> 00:01:19.188
Ricky hugged himself and shivered.

21
00:01:19.188 --> 00:01:22.018
"So you see, son," said Dad.

22
00:01:22.018 --> 00:01:25.881
"It is not easy to live in the Arctic."

23
00:01:25.881 --> 00:01:29.885
"I think I can do it," said Ricky.

24
00:01:29.885 --> 00:01:33.141
"But I need to start training right away.

25
00:01:33.141 --> 00:01:36.465
And I'll need your help."

26
00:01:36.465 --> 00:01:40.932
"All right. What can I do?" asked Dad.

27
00:01:40.932 --> 00:01:46.935
"Can you add five dollars to my weekly allowance?" asked Ricky.

28
00:01:46.935 --> 00:01:50.544
"How will that help?" asked Dad.

29
00:01:50.544 --> 00:01:54.091
"Well," said Ricky.

30
00:01:54.091 --> 00:01:57.740
"I can buy ice cream with the money.

31
00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:05.944
That will help me get used to the cold!"

